## Original Content
The president has told Bank of America and JPMorgan Chase to stop cutting conservatives off from doing business.

## Summary
President Trump has intervened in claims of discrimination by big banks against conservatives, instructing Bank of America and JPMongo Chase to stop cutting them off from business services. This action underscores ongoing concerns about bias in the financial sector and political influence on banking practices.

## Key Points
- President Trump is addressing allegations of big banks discriminating against conservatives.
- He has specifically named Bank of America and JPMorgan Chase in his directive.
- The core issue involves conservatives being denied access to business services by these institutions.
- This move amplifies existing claims of systemic bias within major financial organizations.


